  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 328 AM EDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\n- Dry through Tuesday\n\nHigh confidence in dry fall weather today through Tuesday. BUFKIT\noverviews show little in the way of moisture through the depth of\nthe atmosphere through next Tuesday. Ensemble data from both the\nGFS and ECWMF show no members with any precipitation into next\nTuesday, so 80 members indicating dry. That is an emphatic\nstatement that dry weather will continue into early next week.\n\n- Chances for rain mid next week (Tues night through Wed Night) \n\nMajor model discrepancies arise mid next week when looking at the\nGFS and the ECWMF. The GFS is bringing a deep fall low (989mb) right\nthrough the western Great Lakes during the Tuesday and Wednesday \ntime frame, whereas the ECMWF has some weak surface troughing\n(1012-1014mb). Interestingly, both bring locally heavy \nprecipitation to the area during this time frame. With the GFS the\nrain is driven by the deep low and a strong cold front. In the \nECMWF the rain is driven by overrunning of a warm front. Low \nconfidence to say the least out at this range in the forecast, but\nwe will continue to monitor trends to see if we can get better \nagreement. \n\n- Slightly above normal temperatures through the 7 day forecast\n\nNormal highs for this time of year are in the upper 60s for the\nmost part. MOS guidance and 850 temperatures around +10C indicate\nthat we will likely be a bit above normal for highs in the lower \n70s. Lows will dip into the 40s into next Monday.",
